From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] SystemUI: recents: make the task stack usable with a
 keypad

On devices without a touch panel the keys did nothing useful in the
low-RAM recents:

- no task view had focus after opening, so OK had no target and the
  focus was not shown;
- the D-pad scroll used task indices, while the low-RAM layout scrolls
  in its own units (task i sits at getScrollPForTask(i)), so every arrow
  landed four tasks off and the focused view was not bound;
- DOWN moved the focus to the older task, which the list shows above;
- a long OK acted like a short one.

Give the initial task view focus when there is no touchscreen, convert
the scroll for the low-RAM layout as the touch handler already does,
follow the list direction, draw a frame around the focused task, and
handle OK in RecentsActivity: released it opens the focused task, held
it dismisses it.
